      "excerpt": "Our top 10 customers accounted for 64% of our net revenue for the three months ended October 2, 2026, compared to 73% of our net revenue for the three months ended October 3, 2025. For the three months ended October 2, 2026, two customers accounted for 14% and 13%, respectively, of our net revenue, and for the three months ended October 3, 2025, four customers accounted for 16%, 13%, 13% and 12%, respectively, of our net revenue. 35 Table of Contents Gross Profit and Gross Margin Gross profit increased by $1.31 billion, or 14 percentage points, for the three months ended October 2, 2026 from the comparable period in the prior yea r, due to improved pricing, an increased volume of shipments, and a lower cost structure on our newer generation products. Operating Expenses Research and development expense decreased by $11 million for the three months ended October 2, 2026 from the comparable period in the prior year. The decrease was attributable to lower compensation-related costs. Selling, general and administrative expense increased by $24 million for the three months ended October 2, 2026 from the comparable period in the prior year. The increase was primarily attributable to higher compensation-related costs. For information regarding Business realignment charges, see Part I, Item 1, Note 8, Business Realignment Charges, of the Notes to Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements included in this Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q. Interest and Other Income (Expense) Total interest and other income (expense) changed by $553 million for the three months ended October 2, 2026 from the comparable period in the prior year. The change reflects a non-recurring gain of $611 million on our retained interest in Sandisk in the prior period based on the mark-to-market value as of October 3, 2025, partially offset by lower interest expense of $48 million, which reflects the reduction in our debt. Income Taxes The following table presents our Income tax expense and the effective tax rate: Three Months Ended October 2, 2026 October 3, 2025 ($ in millions) Income before taxes $ 2,038 $ 1,337 Income tax expense 259 155 Effective tax rate 13% 12% The primary drivers of the difference between the effective tax rate and the U.S. Federal statutory rate of 21% for the three months ended October 2, 2026 are the relative mix of earnings and losses by jurisdiction, the deduction for FDDEI, excess tax over book deductions for stock-based compensation, as well as certain tax credits. We maintain tax holidays on a portion of our earnings in the Philippines and Thailand, which are set to expire at various dates from 2029 through 2033.",
